        <body>
            <div xml:id="d222">

                <pb facs="0244" n="174" xml:id="pg174"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/4021: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-17T18:00:00-04:00">August 17, 1934—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:26 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>127. As previously arranged I this afternoon met the Minister for Foreign Affairs
                    and the Brazilian Ambassador.</p>
                <p>At this meeting we received a note dated today addressed to the three of us by
                    the Paraguayan Minister in this city quoting in full the Argentine peace formula
                    and accepting the same “without reservations” in the name of his Government.
                    Copies by next air mail unless otherwise instructed.</p>
                <p>It was felt that the fact of Paraguay’s acceptance would be most confidential to
                    our respective Governments and should not be communicated to the Bolivian
                    Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
